      "page": "portfolio",
      "excerpt": "28DIGITAL Beyond Graduation: Opening the Door to Erasmus for Young Entrepreneurs // 28DIGITAL EIT Digital 28DIGITAL Beyond Graduation: Opening the Door to Erasmus for Young Entrepreneurs Date 4 November 2026 Share Evangelos Marios Kemos [email protected] Europe's small and medium-sized enterprises (SMEs) make up over 99% of all companies on the continent and employ more than 136 million people. Behind that scale sits a simple truth: entrepreneurs learn fastest from other entrepreneurs. That is the idea behind Erasmus for Young Entrepreneurs (EYE), the EU-funded exchange programme that pairs new or aspiring entrepreneurs with experienced business owners across participating countries — and it's an opportunity we want more of our alumni and partners to know about. 28DIGITAL has long championed hands-on, peer-to-peer paths into entrepreneurship, and EYE fits squarely into that mission fit both for our student alumni and startup founders. Salvatore Moccia “ The 28DIGITAL journey doesn't stop at graduation. We are training the digital innovators and entrepreneurs Europe needs, and Erasmus for Young Entrepreneurs is yet another collaboration in that direction — a way for our alumni to keep building, well beyond the classroom, with the support of an experienced entrepreneur abroad. ” – Salvatore Moccia, Chief Education & Skills Officer, 28DIGITAL Since it launched, the programme has"
